","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable.official [71f334935]\nZylann Voxel Tool - Version: 1.6.0 GDExtension (release).release\nOS - Windows 11 25H2\nNVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti (8 GB)\n\n\nWhen using Zylann Voxel Tool and setting Visible Collision Shapes = True, Player collision object is not detected and falls through the Voxel mesh.\n\n\n\n\n### System information\n\nOS - Windows 11 25H2   NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti (8 GB)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using Zylann Voxel Tool and setting Visible Collision Shapes = True, Player collision object is not detected and falls through the Voxel mesh.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a basic 3D Scene\nAdd Voxel Terrain - use either Flat or Wave mesh \nCreate or instance a player character  or any Mesh shape with a collision shape\nPosition the player/shape above the voxel mesh\nAdd a camera ( if not included with player)\nToggle Debug > Visible Collision Shapes\nRun\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nTest project too large to upload due to including Voxel Tool\n\n1) Unzip project and open in Godot 4.6.2\n2) Toggle Debug > Visible Collision Shapes\n3) Run\n4) Toggle Debug > Visible Collision Shapes\n5) Run again\n\nIf using the default Capsule and camera, when Visible = True, you will see the collision shape fall through the floor.\nOtherwise, it will remain stable.\n\nUse this link:  https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UBVfW6Y2BMK2bhlXeCXOaKQi6om1J0K2/view?usp=sharing\n","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users